  "body": "In general events are present tense (e.g. \"focus\", \"click\", not \"focused\", \"clicked\"). But we have some exceptions. We should possibly document why, even if it's just \"legacy reasons\", so that people don't copy past tense events?\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#events-2\r\n\r\n- DOMContentLoaded (obvious legacy)\r\n- rejectionhandled (my bad... although rejectionhandle seems weird)\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#mediaevents\r\n\r\n- emptied\r\n- stalled\r\n- loadedmetadata\r\n- loadeddata\r\n- seeked (maybe to contrast with \"seeking\"?)\r\n- ended\r\n",
